## History

Run records live in `./history/` — one file per run, named `YYYY-MM-DD-<run-id>.md`.

Schema for each history entry (see root `CLAUDE.md` for the full description and exact YAML form):

- `date`: YYYY-MM-DD
- `run_id`: short identifier unique within this skill
- `skill`: skill name
- `actor`: agent name or "human"
- `outcome`: `success` | `partial` | `failure`
- `duration_min`: integer
- `proposed_delta`: free text describing a suggested change to SKILL.md/PROCESS.md, or "none"
- `status`: `open` | `applied` | `rejected`
- `delta_target`: repo-relative file path the delta concerns — OPTIONAL (v0.9.0); enables mechanical triage by `review-history`
- `upstream_pr`: URL of the upstream PR opened for this delta — OPTIONAL (v0.9.0); written by `propose-to-core`
- `root_cause_target`: generator path whose missing constraint permitted the mistake — OPTIONAL (v0.11)
- `mistake_class`: kebab-case mistake-class slug, the occurrence-counting key — OPTIONAL (v0.11)

The entry body is free-form prose: notes, links to artifacts, decisions.

**Additive-forever schema convention (v0.11):** all history/scheduled-run/backlog schema fields are additive-OPTIONAL forever — sweeping skills MUST tolerate absence, and a shipped field is never renamed or repurposed. This is what keeps every vintage of record parseable by every future sweep.

## Scheduled runs

(OPTIONAL — only relevant if this process has the 4 scheduling frontmatter fields set; added v0.6.0.)

Scheduled-run records live in `./scheduled-runs/` — sibling to `./history/`, NOT mixed with it. One file per scheduled invocation, named `YYYY-MM-DD-<run-id>.md`. Manual interactive invocations of this process continue writing to `history/`; scheduled invocations (fired by Claude Code's CronCreate via `/schedule-process`) write to `scheduled-runs/`.

Schema for each scheduled-run entry (template at `shared/templates/scheduled-run.md.tmpl`; superset of the history schema):

- `date`: YYYY-MM-DD
- `run_id`: short identifier unique within this skill (UUID suffix recommended to prevent collisions on concurrent runs)
- `skill`: skill name
- `triggered_by`: literal `schedule` (vs `manual` for history entries — this is the distinguishing field)
- `outcome`: `success` | `partial` | `failure`
- `duration_min`: integer
- `authority_declared`: bracketed list copied from this PROCESS.md's `authority:` frontmatter at run time
- `authority_used`: bracketed list of actions actually taken (best-effort; v1 may equal declared)
- `verification_state`: `unverified` on first run; human edits to `verified` after reviewing output
- `proposed_delta`: free text, or `"none"`
- `status`: `open` | `applied` | `rejected`
- `delta_target`: repo-relative file path the delta concerns — OPTIONAL (v0.9.0)
- `upstream_pr`: URL of the upstream PR opened for this delta — OPTIONAL (v0.9.0)
- `root_cause_target`: generator path — OPTIONAL (v0.11)
- `mistake_class`: mistake-class slug — OPTIONAL (v0.11)

**Distinguishing scheduled vs manual at run time:** the SKILL body should check the invoking prompt for the prelude string `"You are running as a scheduled routine"` (injected by `/schedule-process`). Present → write to `scheduled-runs/`; absent → write to `history/`.
